  "description": "SQL Server for a Rask app: `UseRaskSqlServer(...)`, a drop-in replacement for `UseSqlServer` that registers a `ConnectionOpened` interceptor applying the production session settings (`SET LOCK_TIMEOUT`, `SET XACT_ABORT ON`) to every connection the context opens, sets a client command timeout, and turns on transient-failure retrying. SQLite remains Rask's default; this is the door out when one box is no longer enough. Unlike Rask.SQLite there is no separate raw-ADO package — SqlClient already provides the pooling and transient-retry that Rask.SQLite had to add by hand.",
